{"title":"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 64","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Recursion)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Recursion)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_64&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Alexis and Joshua are walking along the beach when they decide to draw symbols in the sand. Alex draws only stars and only draws them in pairs while Joshua draws only squares in trios. \"Let's see how many rows of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> adjacent symbols we can make this way,\" suggests Josh. Alexis is game for the task and the two get busy drawing. Some of their rows look like \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/e/92e9e43bb103c5309a950410b052102742be8339.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{ccccccccccccccc}\\vspace{10pt}*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;\\blacksquare&amp;\\blacksquare&amp;\\blacksquare\\\\\\vspace{10pt}\\blacksquare&amp;\\blacksquare&amp;\\blacksquare&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*\\\\\\vspace{10pt}\\blacksquare&amp;\\blacksquare&amp;\\blacksquare&amp;\\blacksquare&amp;\\blacksquare&amp;\\blacksquare&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;\\blacksquare&amp;\\blacksquare&amp;\\blacksquare\\\\\\vspace{10pt}\\blacksquare&amp;\\blacksquare&amp;\\blacksquare&amp;\\blacksquare&amp;\\blacksquare&amp;\\blacksquare&amp;\\blacksquare&amp;\\blacksquare&amp;\\blacksquare&amp;\\blacksquare&amp;\\blacksquare&amp;\\blacksquare&amp;\\blacksquare&amp;\\blacksquare&amp;\\blacksquare\\\\\\vspace{10pt}*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;\\blacksquare&amp;\\blacksquare&amp;\\blacksquare&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*\\end{array}\\]\" width=\"438\" height=\"158\" />\n</p><p>The twins decide to count each of the first two rows above as distinct rows, even though one is the mirror image of the other. But the last of the rows above is its own mirror image, so they count it only once. Around an hour later, the twins realized that they had drawn every possible row exactly once using their rules of stars in pairs and squares in trips. How many rows did they draw in the sand? \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_64&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We will use <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Casework\" title=\"Casework\">casework</a> on the number of triplets drawn in order to count the number of rows drawn.\n</p>\n<ul><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triplet is drawn, then there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> pairs needed.  There is a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/a/9eac74f27331cb18476c7aa56642ca4ae7f1ea64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{7}{1} = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"70\" height=\"53\" /> rows in this case.</li>\n<li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triplets are drawn, then there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> pairs needed.  There is a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/4/9e4103126cd01d67e024c33d1752e5318b0273cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{6}{3} = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"79\" height=\"53\" /> rows in this case.</li>\n<li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triplets are drawn, then there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> pairs needed.  There is only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> row in this case.</li></ul>\n<p>Since the twins drew all the possible rows, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/4/9d43f1a642debe75fe4dc442ffb3aa4674b5ff60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7+20+1 = \\boxed{28}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"135\" height=\"23\" /> rows that the twins drew.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Recursion.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Recursion)\">Solution 2 (Recursion)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_64&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Recursion)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> be the amount of valid ways to arrange pairs and trios of symbols. Note that this is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/6/2b6dca444dc8429c2c664b1b928eb77de65e5c64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n-2)+f(n-3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"159\" height=\"20\" />, because both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/9/ef9b02e32cfba0db0f9038a8d077596720f62e91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/5/31503c8c86ff405ea9ae2dd6285eecb04550cb97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> conveniently allow us to add a final pair or trio to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> symbols. Using binomial recursive expansion, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/2/712a9ea08168cad74c0274a11f9a06ea13d6e116.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(15) = f(3)+4f(4)+6f(5)+4f(6)+f(7)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"356\" height=\"20\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/a/3ca6b893b9b50154f494fc050453348c9d91fa22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2) = f(3) = f(4) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"186\" height=\"20\" />, this can be simplified further to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/0/b200bd5511ee4163df9544193ae9388cc4613b62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+4+6(1+1)+4(1+1)+(1+2) = \\boxed{28}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"344\" height=\"25\" />. \n</p><p>~sigma\n</p><p>Note: Recursive binomial expansion is just a fancy way of generalizing a pattern of recursive functions of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/2/ee23a58566dd288a505dd635a8e02997a78f2ec0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)=f(n-k)+f(n-k-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"252\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_64&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest\" title=\"2008 iTest\">2008 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems\">(Problems)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_63\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 63\">Problem 63</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_65\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 65\">Problem 65</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 25\">25</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 26\">26</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 27\">27</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 28\">28</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 29\">29</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 30\">30</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_31\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 31\">31</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_32\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 32\">32</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_33\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 33\">33</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_34\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 34\">34</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_35\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 35\">35</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_36\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 36\">36</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_37\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 37\">37</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_38\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 38\">38</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_39\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 39\">39</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_40\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 40\">40</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_41\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 41\">41</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_42\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 42\">42</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_43\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 43\">43</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_44\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 44\">44</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_45\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 45\">45</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_46\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 46\">46</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_47\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 47\">47</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_48\" title=\"2008 iTes